BT 1 0 0 1 0 95 Tm /F1 9 Tf 13 TL (Up to 74% of mental health diagnoses have their first onset before the age of 24 [1]. Depression and anxiety symptoms) Tj T* (are particularly common among college students, with more than half reporting symptoms of anxiety and depression in) Tj T* (the previous year that were so severe they had difficulty functioning [2]. In addition, epidemiological data suggest that) Tj T* (mental health problems are both increasing in prevalence and severity [3]. However, up to 75% of the college students) Tj T* (that need them do not access clinical services [3]. While the reasons for this are varied, the ubiquity of free or) Tj T* (inexpensive mental health services on campuses suggests that service availability and cost are not primary barriers to) Tj T* (care [3]. Like non-college populations, stigma is considered the primary barrier to accessing psychological health) Tj T* (services.) Tj T* ET
