BT 1 0 0 1 0 95 Tm /F1 9 Tf 13 TL (Using Woebot was associated with a significant reduction in depression as measured by the PHQ-9. The effect size for) Tj T* (depression was moderate though smaller than the four published studies [23-26] that describe three other mobile app) Tj T* (interventions targeting depression. For example, Burns et al [26] found a reduction in depression symptoms with a) Tj T* (between-groups effect size of 1.9, and Watts et al also found significant reductions in PHQ-9 scores with an effect size) Tj T* (of 1.56, both after an 8-week program. However, these interventions were much longer in duration than Woebot, which) Tj T* (was just 2 weeks long. Indeed, our effect size for reduction in depression is in line with that observed in a randomized) Tj T* (trial of DBT Coach [27], a mobile app for individuals with borderline personality disorder, who received a similar dose of) Tj T* (14 days.) Tj T* ET
Q
Q
q
1 0 0 1 59.85827 275.8661 cm
q
0 0 0 rg
BT 1 0 0 1 0 160 Tm /F1 9 Tf 13 TL (The number of participants reporting that the bot felt empathic is noteworthy, and comments that referred to the bot as) Tj T* (\223he,\224 \223a friend,\224 and a \223fun little dude\224 suggest that the perceived source of empathy was Woebot rather than the bot\222s) Tj T* (developers. This is especially noteworthy since a purposefully robotic name \223Woebot\224 was chosen to emphasize the) Tj T* (nonhuman nature of the agent. This is in line with other work that suggests that therapeutic relationship can be) Tj T* (established between humans and nonhuman agents in the context of health and mental health. For example, Bickmore) Tj T* (et al [10] have demonstrated that individuals using a bot to encourage physical activity developed a measurable) Tj T* (therapeutic bond with the conversational agent after 30 days. This embodied bot was built on substantial design work) Tj T* (on establishing human-computer relationships [28]. In addition, a trial that compared therapeutic engagement with a) Tj T* (nonhuman agent between individuals randomized to think that there was a human operating the agent or not) Tj T* (demonstrated that individuals were more willing to disclose to an artificially intelligent \223virtual therapist\224 than when they) Tj T* -0.091052 Tw (believed it was human-operated [29]. The results of this preliminary trial suggest that this should be explored explicitly in) Tj T* 0 Tw (future studies, ideally employing a standardized measure of working alliance, such as the Working Alliance Inventory) Tj T* ([30].) Tj T* ET
Q
Q
q
1 0 0 1 59.85827 151.8661 cm
q
0 0 0 rg
BT 1 0 0 1 0 108 Tm /F1 9 Tf 13 TL (The frequency of process-related comments made by participants in response to questions about their experience with) Tj T* (Woebot suggests that conversational agents can approximate some therapeutic process factors. In addition, just as) Tj T* (these factors are thought to convey much of the variance in positive outcomes across therapeutic approaches, this) Tj T* (study suggests that conversational agent process factors, such as the ability to convey empathy, may be capable of) Tj T* (both amplifying and conversely, violating, a therapeutic process. This underscores the importance of including trained) Tj T* (and seasoned clinicians in clinical app design processes. While this point has been suggested, for example in the) Tj T* (recent guidelines for clinical app evaluation published by the American Psychiatric Association [31], and in the United) Tj T* -0.064052 Tw (Kingdom by the National Institute for Health and Care Excellence [32], this study goes some way towards illustrating the) Tj T* 0 Tw (impact that therapeutic process variables may have on user experience in the context of mental health apps.) Tj T* ET
Q
